From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:13:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dt-bindings: input: gpio-matrix-keypad: add
 linux,capslock-trigger

A board can put its caps lock indicator on a separate LED controller. Let
the keypad accept the caps lock LED state and pass it on as an LED
trigger, so that the indicator follows caps lock whether the console or a
compositor tracks it.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
index 9181ad3a0..1e90eb80b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
@@ -76,6 +76,14 @@ properties:
       interval instead of requesting interrupts for the row GPIOs. Polling
       cannot wake a suspended system.
 
+  linux,capslock-trigger:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The board has a caps lock indicator. The keypad then accepts the caps
+      lock LED state from the input layer and reports it through an LED
+      trigger named after the device, with "-capslock" appended, so that an
+      indicator on another controller can follow it.
+
   held-poll-interval:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     minimum: 1
-- 
